# Cloudflare Pages response headers for static assets.
#
# /cli.ps1 is the Windows installer, fetched as
# `irm https://shiori.nagi.fun/cli.ps1 | iex`. PowerShell's Invoke-RestMethod
# decides between returning a string and returning a byte[] from the response
# content type, and `.ps1` is not in the mime table any static host ships — it
# falls back to application/octet-stream, which iex cannot run. Declaring
# text/plain here is what makes the one-liner work.
#
# The POSIX installer at /cli does not need a rule: it is served by
# site/functions/cli.ts, which sets its own content type.
/cli.ps1
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
